  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">France&apos;s Contribution to the 2022 Refugee and Migrant Response Plan for the Venezuela Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ongoing political and socio-economic developments in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela have led to the outflow of millions of Venezuelans into neighbouring countries and beyond. The Latin America and Caribbean (LAC) region has never experienced, in modern history, such a large-scale movement of both migrants and refugees. In 2015, there were approximately 700,000 Venezuelans living outside their country worldwide. In the last six years, this number has grown nearly nine times as large, to approximately 6.03 million migrants and refugees from Venezuela outside their country worldwide, with 4.99 million (over 80 per cent of all Venezuelans abroad) hosted in LAC as of February 2022. This project is facilitating the ongoing achievement of the Refugee and Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) 2022 objectives, in response to the Venezuelan refugee and migrant situation in Colombia, Ecuador and across LAC through the Regional Office of the Special Envoy. This includes ongoing support to coordination mechanisms and socioeconomic integration in Colombia, child protection and health services to children and adolescents with physical and neurodevelopmental disabilities in Ecuador and access to emergency funds for regional projects through IOM&#x2019;s Regional Office of the Special Envoy (OSE) underfunded grants mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
